{
  "notes": [
    "The four vectors form one chain: the metric summary frame feeds both its own hash and the signing digest; the payload hash feeds the commitment. Regenerating one without its dependents breaks the chain.",
    "metric_summary is the required nested 10-field frame, 138 bytes. Both optional ratios are present here and encode presence in band as 0x01 followed by the framed uint32.",
    "verifier_result_payload_v1 is H_V1 rather than H_FIELDS_V1 and therefore carries payload_hex instead of fields[]: the payload is one opaque FRAME_V1 blob whose own field list is owned by 04-task/04 §9.",
    "Each vector carries mutations[]: one per encodable leaf plus the semantic cases §10.1 names. A mutation only asserts the digest moves or the input is rejected; it never introduces a domain. digest_hex is the value the mutated input produces, so an implementation that ignores a field will reproduce the positive digest and fail here."
  ],
  "schema": "trueopen.task.result_receipt.v2",
  "source": "§5.14 publishes the payload bytes and all three digests; 04-task/§7.1 publishes the MetricSummaryV1 inputs. Authored here because no upstream node fixture covers the V2 result chain.",
